### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The fact-check record shows that Joe Biden explicitly stated he does not want to ban fracking, saying "I am not banning fracking" ([source](https://www.uagetinvolved.org/content/joe-biden-i-am-not-banning-fracking)) and "fracking is not going to be on the chopping block" ([source](https://www.newsweek.com/biden-says-fracking-jobs-wont-chopping-block-if-hes-elected-1516793)). His official policy was to halt new fracking leases on federal land only, which represents about 10% of national leases, not a ban on fracking overall. Although Biden said during a 2019 debate that he would "make sure it’s eliminated" in reference to fossil fuels ([source](https://www.factcheck.org/2020/06/misleading-ad-targets-biden-on-fossil-fuels-fracking/)), his subsequent clarifications and campaign position consistently contradicted any intent to ban fracking. Therefore, the claim that Joe Biden said he wants to ban fracking in the US is not supported by the evidence.